    {
      "anchor": "kvm-servers",
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "KVM Servers"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "device-channel",
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Device channel"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "device-channel",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Device channel is used to specify the controller number and unit number for each attached drive. This is used so every time you reboot your virtual machine, the drive remains on the same place in your guest OS ( ex: /dev/sdc ) You specify the channel in the following format - {controller}:{unit} with the following limits for ide and virtio device types:"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "device-channel",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "ide - 0:0, 0:1, 1:0, 1:1 ( total of 4 drives, max 2 units per controller, i.e 0-1)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "device-channel",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "virtio - 0:0, …, 0:5, …, 1:0, etc ( total of 1024 drives, max 6 units per controller i.e 0-5)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "open-vnc-tunnel",
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Open VNC Tunnel"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "post--servers-uuid-action-?do=open_vnc",
      "kind": "operation",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/api/2.0/servers/{uuid}/action/?do=open_vnc"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "open-vnc-tunnel",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Server’s console (virtual keyboard, mouse, and display) is exposed to the user through the VNC protocol. The open_vnc call opens a VNC tunnel to the server. The returned object contains a vnc_url specifying the endpoint to which to connect the VNC client. The password for the VNC connection is specified in the vnc_password field on the server definition. Note that the tunnel is not closed until reboot, so if you prefer you can close is using the close_vnc action."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "open-vnc-tunnel",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "202 Accepted – Action accepted, execution is proceeding."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "open-vnc-tunnel",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Note"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "open-vnc-tunnel",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "VNC URL will be different each time you close/open the tunnel."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "open-vnc-tunnel",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Example request:"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "open-vnc-tunnel",
      "classification": "request-example",
      "kind": "code",
      "method": "POST",
      "original_sha256": "72de428ab749be50d8593c462e9c78e10411d9e0830a00c4430882afa450da9f",
