    {
      "anchor": "advanced-settings",
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Advanced settings"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "advanced-settings",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "On every server configuration there are a few advanced options you can setup."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "advanced-settings",
      "classification": "unclassified-code",
      "kind": "code",
      "original_sha256": "c60e5e0ccdc463476a30b7bf5bb2f0e434bef74d9968c320882a0b6d76e0eb88"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "advanced-settings",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Type: true/false"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "advanced-settings",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Description: selects whether the SMP is exposed as cores of a single CPU or separate CPUs. This should be set to false for Windows, because there are license requirements for multiple CPUs."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "advanced-settings",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Type: true/false"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "advanced-settings",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Description: This option exposes the NUMA/CPU topology of the hypervisor to the virtual machine. It boosts performance for NUMA aware applications. The option should be set to true for servers with SMP bigger than 6, since this is the number of cores we have per NUMA node on the hypervisor. If set to true, cpus_instead_of_cores should also be set to true for Linux, because some Linux distributions do not support multiple NUMA nodes on multple CPU cores, but only on multiple CPUs."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "advanced-settings",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Type: true/false"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "advanced-settings",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Description: Relax constraints on timers. This improves the behavior of VMs running Windows."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "advanced-settings",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Type: true/false"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "advanced-settings",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Description: Enables more precise timers for Windows. This boost performance for timer specific code."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "advanced-settings",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Warning"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "advanced-settings",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "hv_relaxed and hv_tsc should be set to false for VMs running Linux"
    }
  ],
